    :param modify: The values of the modifiers
    :return: Indicates success or failure of component checks.; Diagnostic message if .NOT. OK."""
    return _context().tcheck(tvec, type, mods, modify)

def terminator_points(method, ilusrc, target, et, fixref, abcorr, corloc, obsrvr, refvec, rolstp, ncuts, schstp, soltol):
    """Terminator points on a target body, without a limit on their number (PEPPER; `termpt` without MAXN). The outputs are allocated to the number of points found.
    
    :param method: the computation method, as for `termpt`
    :param ilusrc: the illumination source
    :param target: the name of the target body
    :param et: the epoch (TDB seconds past J2000)
    :param fixref: the body-fixed, body-centered target body frame
    :param abcorr: the aberration correction
    :param corloc: the aberration correction locus
    :param obsrvr: the name of the observing body
    :param refvec: the reference vector for the cutting half-planes
    :param rolstp: the roll angular step between the cutting half-planes
    :param ncuts: the number of cutting half-planes
    :param schstp: the angular step size for searching (DSK shapes)
    :param soltol: the solution convergence tolerance (DSK shapes)
    :return: the number of points of each cut (size 0 after an error); the terminator points, shape (3, n) (n = 0 after an error); the epochs of the points; the vectors from the observer to the points, shape (3, n)"""
    return _context().terminator_points(method, ilusrc, target, et, fixref, abcorr, corloc, obsrvr, refvec, rolstp, ncuts, schstp, soltol)

def texpyr(year):
